# Do Not Pass Instance Data Back Into Its Own Methods

**Rule:** When a method on a class/model formats or computes something from the object's own fields, use the instance variables directly (ideally as a `get` property) instead of accepting them as parameters. If the data already belongs to the instance, the caller should not have to pass it back.

### ❌ Bad Example
```dart
class RecentSearch {
  final DateTime departureDate;

  String formatDate(DateTime date) => '${date.day}/${date.month}';
}

// Caller passes the instance's own field back into it
final display = item.formatDate(item.departureDate);
```

### ✅ Good Example
```dart
class RecentSearch {
  final DateTime departureDate;

  String get departureDateDisplay =>
      '${departureDate.day}/${departureDate.month}';
}

final display = item.departureDateDisplay;
```
